## 6. What “the exact C3 marginal” refers to

The phrase in BASIN2 points to the earlier **oracle-head marginal**, not the
later set-interaction Ψ unless explicitly redefined. Primary record:
`/home/sat/mcrl-v023-astra-c3core/03-ORACLE-MARGINALS.md:1-5,7-117` reports C3
nonpositive in all four G0--G3 cells (G3 exactly zero). Primary code:
`/home/sat/mcrl-v023-astra-c3core/15-ORACLE-MARGINALS-CODE/oracle_marginals.py`.

Its exact estimator is:

1. For every focal user/action, relative to a reference profile, form
   `delta = candidate_bits - reference_bits`; C1 is focal delta minus
   lambda-times network-energy delta; C3 is the sum of **nonfocal** bit deltas
   (`target_triplet`, `:100-118`). The energy-priced C3 variant is calculated but
   is not the executed C3 surface.
2. C1 and C3 receive exactly one `/kappa`; exact OPS-3 C2 is already
   reference-centred and normalized. `O12 = argmax(C1+C2)` and
   `O123 = argmax(C1+C2+C3)` with masked lowest-action-index ties
   (`compose_actions`, `:121-166`). O12/O123 therefore do not require learned
   Q1/Q2, although the same historical script also produced learned hybrid arms.
3. The reference profile/action and all unilateral candidates are consumed at
   `_one_step_surfaces` (`:282-309`). Historical BASE is reconstructed/checked at
   `:357-371`; complete composed arms are physically evaluated at `:382-410`.
4. C3 marginal is `pooled_EE(O123) - pooled_EE(O12)`, strict positive iff the
   former is greater (`MARGINALS` at `:63-64`; summarizer `:461-496`). The four
   original cells are `G0` full buffer and G1/G2/G3 demand caps of 200/50/10
   Mbit/s/user (`:58-64`, `:86-97`).

BASIN2's global rule says full-buffer numerator/no demand cap, while Part 4 says
“sign per cell.” The historical `03-ORACLE-MARGINALS` meaning of cell is G0--G3,
but only G0 obeys the new global no-cap rule. This is a specification ambiguity
the implementation must resolve explicitly; do not silently run capped G1--G3.
If “cell” instead means each of the 12 BASIN anchors, report each anchor's
full-buffer O123-vs-O12 direction and say this is an anchorwise adaptation of the
historical pooled estimator. In either reading, only the reference changes from
BASE to RSS_MAX; retain the target, normalization, masked argmax, tie, physical
endpoint, and pooled-ratio definitions.

There is a second, conceptually relevant but different V0.25 quantity:
`Psi_A^r = [F(full)-F(r)] - sum_i[F(singleton_i)-F(r)]`. Its canonical exact
implementation is
`/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/src/mcrl/physics_v025/targets.py:424-448,451-535`:
it requires the reference, every singleton substitution, and the complete
coalition; computes every value as exact `bits - eta*joules`; and returns
`C3=Psi/kappa` while asserting `C1+C3=joint/kappa`. The explicitly learner-free
re-anchoring probe is
`/home/sat/mcrl-v025-probe-ws/.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/probe/probe_interaction_existence.py:1-19,442-510,562-628`.
It builds a bounded joint neighbourhood around either `a0` or a unilateral
optimum and records `psi_bits`. Its evaluator calls do not meet BASIN2's clean
rule (scalar reads at `:484,497,506,574,586`), so borrow only its definition and
candidate-estimator shape.

Do not conflate these quantities. The phrase “exact C3 oracle-marginals
negative in every cell” is a literal title/table match for the historical
policy-level `EE(O123)-EE(O12)` estimator above; the basin/joint-move motivation
is a conceptual match for `Psi_A^r`. KILLTRIAGE itself says the historical
oracle marginal priced a narrower unilateral object and cannot bear a broader
set-coordination claim
(`/home/sat/mcrl-v025-triage-ws/KILL-TRIAGE-2026-09-10.md:50-52,104-106`).
The BASIN driver/report must name which of the two it recomputes rather than
silently labelling one as the other. Moreover, the pilot `_exact_interactions`
path for V0.25 Psi is known mixed:
`/home/sat/mcrl-v025-probe-ws/EVALPATH-2026-09-10.md:102-107`.

The historical probe's reference dependence is structural: all unilateral
delta surfaces are explicitly measured relative to `reference_profile` and
`reference_actions` (`oracle_marginals.py:282-309`). Therefore a sign change
under RSS_MAX would justify exactly the requested scope sentence only: **the
sign of the exact interaction marginal depends on the reference profile. This
is a statement about the earlier probe's scope, not a revival.**

