  candidates together**. Assert call count, batch membership, `(0,)`, dense
  arrays, and `a-r0` before reading `_evaluated`.
- Monkeypatch scalar `StepEvaluator.evaluate` to raise; assert zero calls at end.
- Use `_evaluated` only after dense population; remember `evaluate_many` itself
  falls back to scalar if arrays are absent or setting is not `a-r0`
  (`run_v025_matrix_probe.py:796-801`), so assert both preconditions.
- Endpoint: one separate fresh realised full-48 evaluator per anchor; one batch
  call containing every profile whose endpoint values/orders are compared.
- Preserve exact `Fraction` F for barrier/order comparisons and trajectory;
  compute pooled EE separately from full-buffer bits and joules.
- Hamming/path candidates and k-user simultaneous subsets are changes toward
  RSS_MAX only. Guard them against the same dense reference served count.
- Keep the published values beside clean values and differences; never use
  13.430253 or 28.668530 as parity requirements.
- No loss/checkpoint evidence. O12/O123 in the oracle C3 estimator can be built
  from exact C1/C2/C3 surfaces without reading learned Q1/Q2.
- Print `anchor k/N`, peak RSS, process/thread/niceness assertions, and stay under
  the user's 3-process/5-GB limits.

## Classification

Verified by direct source/report reading: all cited control flow, constants,
stored published measurements, evaluator defect, and the live rank2 status.

Derived on paper: the compliant driver requirements obtained by combining the
cache semantics with BASIN2's stricter batch clause; the fact that STATICS2's
selection warm-up is not literally sufficient; the exact interpretation of an
ascending BASE-to-RSS path.

Inferred / unresolved: whether Part 4's “cell” means historical demand grids or
the 12 anchors. The source evidence supports both vocabulary uses; the new
full-buffer rule conflicts with silently reproducing capped G1--G3.

